WEBVTT

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.060
Maku... nouchi...

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.060
My... hand...

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.070
Baton...

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.940
pass.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.080
It's... yours now.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:33.750
I see.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.090
So the old man said something like that.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:38.080
Yes.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:44.850
Date-san's really going to retire.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:49.690
Now we have no one to lead the world of Japanese Boxing.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:50.930
Well, we've got somebody.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.270
The guy who had the baton officially passed on to him.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.950
M-Me?

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.620
T-There's no way I could do that.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.120
You got that right.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.620
You're not dignified enough.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.620
I wouldn't want you to lead.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:12.210
<i>Then don't say anything in the first place.</i>

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:16.160
You should just focus on your own business for now.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:19.510
You've got your second title defense coming up, right?

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:20.630
Uh... {Solo-  I know we usually don't tl stuff like this but it is a clear word...}

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:21.930
what was his name again?

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:23.930
It's "Hammer Nao!"

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:27.680
The guy who got ranked 7th in the featherweights practically overnight?

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.520
Never heard of him.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:33.480
I might not have much information to go off of, 
but I'll still do my best!

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.270
I'll just take each title defense one step at a time.

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:40.030
That's all there is for me to do right now!

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.130
Whew, he's really going at it today!

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:55.710
He's really into it.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:01:59.720
Take a break!

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.090
You're relying too much on power!

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.800
You've got to choose your shots more carefully!

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:06.390
Right!

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:10.480
Well, it's good that you're putting some spirit into it.  {Solo-  Suggest a line split}

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.900
R-Right...

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.400
I guess it's because I saw Date-san trying so hard.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.740
He showed incredible fighting spirit.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:19.900
It's a shame that he's retiring.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:24.310
Those of you who succeed him have a lot to live up to.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:28.570
If you want to follow Date, then you need to focus on not botching these title defenses.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.160
Don't underestimate Hammer Nao.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.000
I understand!

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.420
There's nothing scarier than not knowing about your opponent.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:37.920
What?

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:58.020
I thought so.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:02:59.980
I was wondering who was making those sweet sounds.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.860
I should have known it was Makunouchi-senpai.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:06.110
Hey, hey! How long are you gonna stand there? 
Close the door already!

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:08.830
If you're here to check the place out, then go take a seat.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:10.900
Check it out, huh?

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.830
Well, I planned to join, but...

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:15.870
Um...

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.230
Who're you guys?

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.920
You mean to tell me that you're joining this gym and you don't know who we are!?

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.550
You're starting to get on my nerves.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:25.550
Really?

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:28.510
We just met and I already don't like you!

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:26.680
What are they doing?

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.140
Looks like they're arguing about something.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:31.640
Now, now... don't get so upset...

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.640
W-Why you...

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.390
Ah, there you are!  {Solo-  Not sure about the "ah"}

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:35.430
Yagi-san!

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.440
Yagi-san, you know this guy?

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.400
Allow me to introduce you!

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.900
This is last year's inter-high national runner-up.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:46.860
He's the rookie our gym has high hopes for, Itagaki Manabu-kun!

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:47.410
Nice to meet you.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.490
Huh?

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:54.910
They don't look happy to see me, do they?

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:57.370
One of the boxing amateur elites, huh?

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.420
So you scouted this guy, Yagi-san?

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:05.170
Well, actually he had already entered college and joined the boxing club there, but...

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:09.220
...something about hitting people through their headgear didn't suit me.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.930
He contacted me when I started thinking about becoming a pro.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.560
Besides, this gym has a boxer that I idolize,

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.310
so I thought I'd come see what I could learn!

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:17.560
Idolize?

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.350
Boxer?

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:21.060
You're accepted!

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.360
It's Takamura!

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.020
That's right!

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:31.070
It is I, your idol, Takamura Mamoru!

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:35.500
Watch me closely every day and learn how it's done.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.290
Actually, Takamura-kun, that's not it.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:41.990
Itagaki-kun is a featherweight, so he looks up to...

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.340
What!?

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.920
He looks up to Ippo!?

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.590
M-Me?

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:52.550
What about his boneheaded boxing is appealing to you!?

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:54.970
If I was a featherweight, I'd look up to Sendo...

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:57.310
or maybe Saeki, he was an amateur boxer as well.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.140
Sanada's good too!

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.100
You guys do realize that...

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:04.060
all those guys have lost to Ippo, right?

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:06.780
And so...

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.650
I'll be counting on your help,

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:10.160
Makunouchi-senpai!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.320
O-Oh...

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:12.280
the pleasure's all mine.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.580
Well, in that case...

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:16.950
How about our traditional roadwork welcoming for newbies?

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:17.950
Roadwork?

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:22.460
It's the fastest way to show him how tough being a pro is, isn't it?

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:25.000
Oh, yeah.

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:31.970
S-Senpai,

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.140
you're going too fast!

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.810
Do you always run at this pace!?

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:37.970
S-Sorry!

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.130
Should I slow down?

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:43.020
He's giving up, just like we figured.

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:47.280
This is what being a pro is like, he'll be puking from the pain in no time.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.360
Dumbasses!

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.360
You're the ones about to puke!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.860
They're way ahead of you!

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:57.240
Inter-high national runner-up ain't a name that's just for show.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.870
It means he's got his basic conditioning down.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.460
You think he's any good?

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:03.880
Based on his background, he'd probably hold his own pretty well if he went pro right now.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:08.670
But you know... Hearing you guys talking about puking... {Solo-  Split maybe?}

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.670
It's kind of a nostalgic thought, isn't it?

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.260
Oh, yeah!

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:15.890
There was another guy who used to cling to Ippo like that too.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.350
<i>Senpai!</i>

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:28.650
I wonder what he's up to now.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:32.650
It's been about two years since then, you think he's still boxing?

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:35.950
Maybe we beat him up too badly at the send off party?

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:38.660
You were the only one who went overboard!

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:43.290
There's something about Ippo's boxing that seems to attract people to him.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:47.420
He's going to draw in more and more young guys like Itagaki.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:51.010
Before you know it, he might actually be able to fill in for Date-san.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:51.880
Yeah! {jama: added}

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:53.800
I doubt that.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.610
We're back!

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.310
You're here.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.100
Kid, follow me.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:07.110
We've got a video of Hammer Nao.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:08.900
We've got a video?

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:09.570
Let's watch it!

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:13.480
Although I thought you would have found out by now...

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:17.160
"Hammer Nao."

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.830
He's from the Hachinohe Boxing Club.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:22.290
8 matches, 8 wins, 5 KO's.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.740
He specializes in body hooks.

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:29.380
That was bad enough to make him keel over.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:30.630
It looks pretty heavy.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.550
It should be, considering that he debuted as a junior welterweight.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:36.510
A junior welterweight!?

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:38.550
That's four weight classes up!

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:39.760
He fought two fights there,

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:41.560
went down to lightweight for three matches,

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.270
and then had three matches as a junior lightweight.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:47.270
It seems he dropped down to featherweight because he wanted a match against Ippo-kun.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:49.230
With me?

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:53.100
Have you figured it out yet, Kid?

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:55.740
He may have shaved his head and eyebrows...

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:59.740
His face may be a bit swollen now...

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:03.750
And he might have lost so much weight that you can see his ribs and he barely resembles his former self...

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.420
but he's someone you know very well.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.790
He was formerly a member of this gym.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:12.300
No way.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.260
His real name is...

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:15.540
Yamada Naomichi.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.680
That's Gero-michi!?

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:23.890
No way in hell!

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.890
That can't be Gero-michi!

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:27.390
I mean, he's so scary looking!

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:29.520
If I saw him in the street, I'd get out of the way!

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:31.520
B-But still, if you look closely...

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:33.530
His nose...

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.030
and his mouth...

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:36.530
He's got Yamada-kun's features!

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:38.030
True.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.820
He did carry a lot of water weight.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:42.820
I guess after going through all that weight loss, that's what he looks like.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.080
No way!

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:51.000
There's no way human beings can transform like this!

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.250
I don't buy it!

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.290
Shut it!

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:56.800
Whether you believe it or not,

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.050
that is the one and only Yamada Naomichi.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:01.890
It really is him.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.140
It doesn't even feel nostalgic.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:05.810
He's like a totally different guy.

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:21.660
It really is him.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.870
It doesn't even feel nostalgic.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.580
He's like a totally different guy.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.920
Uh, excuse me, but...

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:34.170
what's a "Gero-michi?"

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:36.760
That's right, Itagaki-kun wouldn't know.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.970
A full explanation would take a while, but...

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:41.510
When we first met him, he puked.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:44.010
When he left, he puked.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:46.970
Naomichi led a life covered in puke.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.930
Hence the name "Gero-michi."

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:51.060
Note: "gero" means "puke."

00:09:48.930 --> 00:09:51.060
That sure is a gross nickname.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:52.650
Who gave it to him?

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:53.810
Who can say?

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:56.360
He was Gero-michi long before we met him.

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:57.820
It remains a wonder who said it first.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:58.990
<i>It was you.</i>

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:00.990
Well, regardless of his nickname...

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:03.990
he gets hit too much.

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:07.330
If he takes that many hits from Makunouchi-senpai, he won't just be KO'd,

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:09.450
he'll end up in the hospital.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:11.000
Seems like an easy win.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.490
I'll be borrowing the video.

00:10:21.590 --> 00:10:24.010
To think that Gero-michi would...

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:26.640
After the way he used to cling to Ippo as his goal.

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:30.310
Maybe he thinks he caught up and that's why he's challenging him?

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:31.980
So he's confident that he'll win?

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.350
That can't be it.

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:35.690
Ippo's grown in the last two years too.

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:38.150
I can't believe that he's made up for that difference.

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.400
Maybe not in terms of strength...

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:42.450
What do you mean?

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:44.320
Exactly what I said.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:48.450
You guys were talking about whether Ippo could follow in the old man's footsteps right?

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:50.150
Yeah...

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:56.170
Before Ippo can take the old man's place, 
he has to correct something he's lacking in.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:58.090
You could even call it a weakness.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.550
Weakness!?

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:02.840
But Ippo has the power to end things with a single punch...

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:05.220
and enough stamina to last into the later rounds.

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:08.680
It'd be hard to find someone at the national level who could stand up to him.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:10.680
He lacks stability.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:14.600
He's never able to fully capitalize on his strengths unless he's in trouble.

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:18.310
That mental naiveté keeps him from fighting ruthlessly from the start.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:21.860
I guess he does let the other guy set the pace and get away with a lot.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:25.160
Yeah, for a boxer, he's too soft and emotional.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:28.580
That might be part of why he's so unstable.

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:31.450
In this world, it's kill or be killed.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:36.120
It shouldn't matter who your opponent is, 
you have to beat them once you set foot in the ring.

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:40.920
Unless you can throw a punch in cold blood, you'll never get the respect that it takes to be seen as the leader.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:42.130
In this next match...

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:47.390
After succeeding in his first title defense, how will the champion win this time?

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:50.850
How will he deal with this fight that he will obviously win?

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:54.110
In many ways, this battle will answer a lot of things.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.110
What's wrong, Aoki?

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.360
I just realized something terrible.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:11.080
In Ippo's next title match,
 I'm fighting in the match right before his.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:12.620
S-So?

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:14.120
It means that...

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:18.750
It's not just for Ippo, I'm the opening act for Gero-michi too!

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:25.630
O-Opening for two of your kouhai...

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:27.630
That's gotta be rough.

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:28.460
Yeah. {jama: added}

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:39.270
<i>Don't rush it.</i>

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:40.610
<i>That left is bait.</i>

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:42.110
<i>Keep your guard up.</i>

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:44.360
<i>That's it! Bit by bit, down below...</i>

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.360
<i>Yeah, that's right!</i>

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:48.360
<i>Yes!</i>

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:50.310
<i>That shot to the body had a good angle!</i>

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:53.860
<i>He's gotten a lot tougher.</i>

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.830
<i>A flat-footed fighter like Yamada-kun isn't good at chasing someone down.</i>

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:02.740
<i>That's why he lets people punch him, to lure them in so he can hammer on them!</i>

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:05.880
<i>It's a strategy that takes a lot of courage.</i>

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:07.840
<i>Senpai...</i>

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:09.930
<i>I get picked on a lot.</i>

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:12.010
<i>How was it?</i>

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:15.140
<i>I tried my very best.</i>

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:16.640
<i>Yamada-kun...</i>

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:20.140
<i>The first kouhai I had at the gym.</i>

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:26.320
<i>He was clumsy and awkward, but tried so hard.</i>

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:33.490
<i>But his family had to move away because of work.</i>

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:35.490
<i>Yamada-kun!</i>

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:37.750
<i>You're going to keep boxing, right!?</i>

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.790
<i>Let's both do our best!</i>

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:42.200
<i>Right!</i>

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:45.120
<i>Thank you so much!</i>

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:50.170
<i>He's good at close range.</i>

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:52.140
<i>It suits how powerful he looks.</i>

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:52.680
<i>But...</i>

00:13:54.470 --> 00:13:57.220
<i>He always ducks to the left when there's a right...</i>

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:58.930
<i>to aim for his specialty, a body blow.</i>

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:00.940
<i>So I'd aim for that.</i>

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:04.940
<i>A left to his open temple and, while he's off balance, a double...</i>

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:08.940
<i>left... then what would I do with it?</i>

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:10.950
<i>Senpai!</i>

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:13.950
<i>Would I hit Yamada-kun?</i>

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:24.000
<i>He kept boxing...</i>

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.740
<i>and got stronger.</i>

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:30.830
<i>Yamada-kun!</i>

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.880
<i>Why did you challenge me?</i>

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:46.730
You okay, Coach!?

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:50.490
Dang, you got a lot of power, Nao.

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:53.820
Looks like you're in good shape... so we can get our hopes up.

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:55.700
You're our first main eventer!

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.270
Good luck, Nao!

00:14:57.740 --> 00:14:58.490
Right.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.740
I'll be heading home.

00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:07.420
The sign, huh?

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.550
Guess we oughta look into getting a new one.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:11.840
I-If I win the title,

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:13.580
I'll be sure to start bringing the money in.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:18.800
I don't want you fighting the title match thinking like that.

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:23.690
You've done really well in a small town gym like this where we've had trouble finding you sparring partners.

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:27.150
I would have liked for you to go at an easier pace.

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:30.270
Build up your experience, carefully raise you up,

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:32.690
and then challenge for the title.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:34.400
Coach...

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:36.910
Why's it gotta be Makunouchi Ippo!?

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:40.790
There was a fighter at this gym named Jason Ozuma!

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:44.990
He was talented, worked hard, and I was sure he could take the title.

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:49.170
But Makunouchi overpowered him.

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:52.840
He's strong... too strong.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:57.180
That fight ended 2 minutes and 54 seconds into the second round, right?

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:01.100
I know how strong Makunouchi Ippo is better than anyone else.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.310
Then why!?

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:04.180
Why would you take him on knowing how dangerous he is!?

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:07.010
Have you ever thought about it like this...

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:10.730
that because I know him, I'm able to overcome him?

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:16.070
When you came to this gym, you said you were boxing because you looked up to Makunouchi Ippo!

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:18.780
Even if you know how to,

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:24.580
are you really gonna be able to beat up the same person you looked up to using those hands!?

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.030
I can.

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:32.790
I can and I will beat him down.

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:40.800
He's as impressive as ever!

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:41.800
Really?

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:43.930
Right here!

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:46.520
Hammer Nao leaves this spot open when he finishes a punch!

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:47.640
Get it!

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:57.360
That's it!

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:00.240
There's no point in holding up these mitts when you're so out of it!

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:02.240
Get your head back together by tomorrow!

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:03.530
Got it!?

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:08.460
He must've seen Gero-michi's face.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:11.500
At this rate, he won't be able to punch ruthlessly.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:14.300
But Gero-michi was pretty emotional too.

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:16.010
Imagine if he couldn't fight properly either.

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:18.010
It doesn't look that way.

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:20.010
Hey, Mari-san!

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:22.010
He really seemed to be in the swing of things.

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:23.510
You went all the way to Aomori?

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:27.020
Gero-michi is in Tokyo!?

00:17:27.430 --> 00:17:29.230
Yamada-kun is in town!?{jama: added}

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:31.310
A training trip to the Nerima Boxing Club.

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:34.690
Man, that's so cold! He could at least come by and say hello.

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:36.320
Why would he?

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.490
Right now, this is enemy territory for him.

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:41.200
Oh, that's got nothing to do with us.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.530
The one picking on Gero-michi is this guy.

00:17:43.530 --> 00:17:45.730
I don't like how they're making that sound.

00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:49.200
Have a good night!

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:51.670
Ippo-kun!

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:56.050
I've been gathering information on Hammer Nao.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:57.410
Would you like to hear it?

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:00.050
Yes, please.

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:06.430
Why are we sneaking around?

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:09.060
Well, he is the enemy, you know.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:12.600
We're just coming to check out how our old kouhai is doing.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:16.070
Now, where is Gero-michi-kun?

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:24.070
Next! Get into the ring!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.030
G-Gero-michi...

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:27.450
...just made someone puke!

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:46.260
In the end, he ended up knocking down three guys in a row...

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:48.140
...and all three of them puked.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:50.680
Anybody would puke after being nailed with body blows like that.

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:52.310
He sure picked up a hell of a weapon.

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:54.270
I'm going to run for a bit.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:55.760
Be careful.

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:05.320
Yo, long time no see, Gero-michi!

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:08.030
We saw you at work there, you've gotten a lot better!

00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:10.330
Are you spying on me?

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:13.120
Come on, don't be like that.

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:16.830
We came to see you because we heard you were in town.

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:18.340
To see me?

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:21.460
I didn't ask you to.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:23.800
I've got running to do, so...

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:25.250
H-Hey!

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:26.840
What?

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:30.560
Could you not glare at us with that face?

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:33.480
You've changed a lot and we're having some trouble dealing with it.

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:37.480
We can't really cheer for you in this match,

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:41.940
but we still wanted to wish you good luck!

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:43.240
Aoki-san,

00:19:43.690 --> 00:19:46.490
just make sure you don't cool off the audience too much when you open for us.

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:51.450
What was that crap!?

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:54.000
Don't think you can get carried away just because you're so ugly now, got it!?

00:19:57.170 --> 00:20:00.290
I'd appreciate it if you stopped acting like my senpai.

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:03.420
I'm not a member of the Kamogawa Gym anymore.

00:20:03.420 --> 00:20:04.220
Why, you little...

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.680
Aoki!

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:06.760
Look Gero-michi,

00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:09.260
stop acting like an asshole.

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:12.390
I understand what you're going through because I fought that monster, Mashiba.

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:16.770
I know you have to psyche yourself up because you're scared.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:19.810
From your point of view, Ippo's a real monster.

00:20:19.810 --> 00:20:21.190
We get it.

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:22.900
When you're around us, you can just be honest.

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:24.400
So you were scared?

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:25.990
No wonder you lost.

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:26.780
What was that!?

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:30.780
Tell Makunouchi Ippo this...

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:32.790
I'm coming

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:37.360
for his belt.
